- `telephone` — `@NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", ...)` (stored in E.164 form)
- `email` (nullable)
- `registrationDate` (LocalDate; defaulted/rolled to business day in `@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()`)
- `customerCode`, `householdId` (`@Column(name="household_id")`), `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`
- `pets` (`@OneToMany`)
- **No `identityKey` / `normalizedTelephone` field exists.**

Derived getters (no backing column): `getLocality()`, `getMembershipNumber()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, `getContactPreference()`.

`Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`) supplies `firstName`, `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`) and `getInitials()`.

## 2 & 3. Creation + duplicate detection (HTTP 409)

All creation logic lives in `addOwner` in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (lines 135-177). `OwnerRestControllerV2.java` only has a paged list endpoint — no create. The duplicate-check core:

```java
String telephone = TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone());
if (!this.clinicService.findOwnerByTelephone(telephone).isEmpty()) {
    throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
}
String email = EmailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail());
if (email != null && !this.clinicService.findOwnerByEmail(email).isEmpty()) {
    throw new DuplicateEmailException(email);
}
Collection<Owner> household =
    this.clinicService.findOwnersInHousehold(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
if (!household.isEmpty() && !sharesHousehold) {
    throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
}
owner.setTelephone(telephone);
owner.setEmail(email);
if (sharesHousehold) {
    this.clinicService.joinHousehold(owner, household);
}
this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
```

The method also validates missing fields (`MissingOwnerFieldsException` → 400), city capacity (`CityCapacityExceededException` → 409, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY=50`), and daily limit (`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` → 429, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY=100`). On success returns `201 CREATED` with a `Location` header.

**Exception → HTTP mapping** in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`. All three duplicate handlers return `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) via a `ProblemDetail`:
- `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409, `errors: ["telephone"]`, detail "An owner with the given telephone number already exists"
- `DuplicateEmailException` → 409, `errors: ["email"]`
- `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409, `errors: ["lastName","address"]`
- `InvalidTelephoneException` → 400, `errors: ["telephone"]`

Exception classes (all in `.../rest/validation/`): `DuplicateTelephoneException.java`, `DuplicateEmailException.java`, `DuplicateHouseholdException.java`, `InvalidTelephoneException.java` — each `extends RuntimeException` and carries the offending value(s).

### Service layer
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (interface `ClinicService.java`):
- `findOwnerByTelephone(telephone)` → `ownerRepository.findByTelephone(telephone)`
- `findOwnerByEmail(email)` → `ownerRepository.findByEmailIgnoreCase(email)`
- `findOwnersInHousehold(lastName, address)` (lines 289-298): loads by `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`, then filters in-memory using `TextNormalizer.normalizeForComparison` on both last name and address.
- `joinHousehold(owner, existingMembers)` (lines 300-312): computes `HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, address)` and stamps it on the new owner and all existing members.

## 4. Telephone normalization

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/TelephoneNormalizer.java` — `normalize(String)` produces canonical E.164. Strips non-digits; preserves `+`/country code if present, else assumes default `+61` and drops a leading `0`. Requires 8-15 digits total; enforces per-country national length (`+61`→9, `+1`→10). Throws `InvalidTelephoneException` on failure. There is **no field named `normalizedTelephone`** — the normalized value is just written back onto `owner.telephone`.

Related normalizers: `EmailNormalizer.java` (lower-cases, null when blank), `AddressNormalizer.java`, and `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/TextNormalizer.java` (`normalizeForComparison`: trims, collapses whitespace, lower-cases — used for household comparison and by `HouseholdIdGenerator`).

## 5. Tests

Only three test files exist, all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

- **`AcceptanceTest.java`** — the sole active test. Class comment: `/** identity-key: Consolidate all duplicate detection into a single derived 'identityKey' = normalizedTeleph... */`. One test:
  ```java
  @Test
  void coreRejectsIdentityCollision() throws Exception {
      ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
      createOwnerOk(a);
      ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
      b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
      createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict()); // same identityKey
  }
  ```
  It creates a unique owner, then a second owner identical only in telephone, and expects 409. This is the target behavior for the not-yet-built `identityKey` feature.

- **`AcceptanceBase.java`** — black-box base (`@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN",...})`). Helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid payload), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`, `getOwner`/`fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, unique generators (`uniqueTelephone()` = `"04%08d"`, `uniqueEmail`, etc.), plus pinned reference data and `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` helpers. Notably references not-yet-implemented features: `Idempotency-Key` header, soft-delete semantics, structured address, postcode.

- **`AuditLogCapture.java`** — audit-log test support.

There are **no unit tests** for `TelephoneNormalizer`, the controller, or the individual duplicate exceptions.

## 6. Owner repository

Interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`. Duplicate-relevant methods: `findByTelephone(String)`, `findByEmailIgnoreCase(String)`, `findByLastNameIgnoreCase(String)`, `findByLastName(...)`, `countByCity`, `countByRegistrationDate`, `save`, `findById`, `findAll`, `delete`.

Three implementations exist: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (Spring Data, active), plus `jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` and `jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`.

## 7. Response structure (client-facing)

DTOs are **generated at build time from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (no hand-written `OwnerDto.java`/`OwnerFieldsDto.java`); mapping via `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct, `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, `toOwnerDto(Owner)` with a computed `displayName`).

- **Request DTO `OwnerFields`** (openapi.yml line 1991): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `registrationDate`, `sharesHousehold` (boolean, default false, not persisted — the household-override opt-in). Required: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.
- **Response DTO `Owner`** (line 2062, allOf OwnerFields + ): `id`, `displayName`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `householdId`, `initials`, `locality`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference` (EMAIL/PHONE), `pets`. (`householdSize` exists on the entity but is **not** exposed in the DTO.)

Error responses use Spring `ProblemDetail` (RFC 7807) with `title` = exception simple name, `detail` = human message, and extra properties `timestamp`, `schemaValidationErrors`, and `errors` (array of offending field names).

## Key takeaway for the "identityKey" feature
The failing `AcceptanceTest` expects duplicate detection to be driven by a single derived `identityKey` (based on normalized telephone). Today that logic is spread across three inline checks in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, three exception types, three advice handlers, and repository lookups (`findByTelephone`, `findByEmailIgnoreCase`). There is currently no `identityKey`/`normalizedTelephone` column, entity field, DTO field, or repository method — only the normalized telephone written back onto `owner.telephone`.

